## Model card

- **Name:** Exo Free
- **Short description:** An anonymous, unannounced free reasoning model that appeared on OpenCode Zen (catalog id `opencode/exo-free`) around October 6, 2026. The publishing lab is undisclosed; a third-party fingerprint probe matched its generation patterns to Claude Opus 5.5 at 99.4% confidence, but that is closed-set community evidence, not vendor verification (candidate theories: confidential blind evaluation, routing misconfiguration, or a distilled clone — none confirmed).
- **Provider / access:** OpenCode Zen `opencode/exo-free` — endpoint `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/chat/completions` (Chat Completions API), also listed at `https://opencode.ai/zen/v1/models`. High traffic has caused frequent "Endpoint is unavailable" notices and 429s; a community poll (68% of 50 votes) said it still worked as of the discovery week.
- **Release / knowledge:** appeared 2026-10-06 (models.dev first observed 2026-10-06 22:54 UTC); knowledge cutoff unknown (undisclosed model).
- **IDs:** `opencode/exo-free` (Free ID on Zen — $0 during the limited free period; no end date announced; requests during the free period may be used to improve the model — no zero-data-retention guarantee).
- **Context window:** ~1M tokens — 1,048,576 total per models.dev (artificialwatch radar), "about a million" per AI Promo Now; max output ~131K tokens (AI Promo Now). Verified via catalog trackers, not a model card.
- **Modalities:** text out; image input accepted; tool calls supported; reasoning effort fixed at high (AI Promo Now briefing). 
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-09):** $0 / $0 per 1M tokens, cached input $0 (LLMRates.ai, AI Promo Now, artificialwatch) — limited-time free with data-training caveat.
- **Architecture:** undisclosed (stealth). No parameter, license, or base-model evidence; the 99.4% Opus 5.5 fingerprint is a generation-pattern match, not a weights identity.

