## Evidence notes

- Zero verified public benchmark numbers for the exact model/ID: every measured row above is either absent or a pass/fail qualitative report; the only numeric result (99.4% fingerprint) measures stylistic similarity, not capability. Standardized scores (SWE-bench, GPQA, Terminal-Bench, AA Intelligence Index) do not exist for Exo Free as of 2026-10-09.
- Scoring an undisclosed stealth model would require either inventing numbers (forbidden) or borrowing another model's scores (forbidden — the fingerprint match is not an identity). Self-exclusion per the template's mandatory SELF-EXCLUSION rule.
- Practical caveats from the sources: extreme availability volatility (429s, dropouts), no zero-data-retention guarantee (prompts and screenshots may train future models — never send proprietary code), and do not rely on the endpoint for production work.

